This repository carries three licences across four kinds of content. Which one
applies is decided by path, not by file type:

1. SOURCE CODE — everything except the three carve-outs below: components,
   layouts, styles, configuration, build pipeline, scripts, and the prose of
   this file itself. Licensed MIT. Full text below.

2. WRITTEN CONTENT — all prose published on the site: the `posts` and
   `projects` collections (`src/content/posts/**/*.mdx` and
   `src/content/projects/**/*.mdx`, frontmatter and body alike), and the
   reader-facing copy in `src/pages/` (the About page, index ledes, page
   descriptions). The markup and code around that copy stay under MIT.
   Licensed CC BY-NC 4.0. Notice below.

3. PHOTOGRAPHS — the image files under `src/assets/photos/`, and any copy or
   derivative Astro generates from them at build time (resized, re-encoded,
   or otherwise transformed versions served from the built site). All rights
   reserved. Notice below.

4. AI IMAGES — the image files under `src/assets/generated/`, and any copy or
   derivative Astro generates from them at build time. Some are a model's
   output as it came; most are composites, generated art arranged and
   finished by hand. Each one carries a visible label saying which. Licensed
   CC BY-NC 4.0, to the extent any copyright subsists in them. Notice below.

If a future file doesn't obviously fall under one of these paths, treat it as
source code unless it's clearly someone's photograph or someone's prose.

